# Godparents, read from the register scans this archive holds.
# Read 13 September 2026 at 3-4x from the full-resolution files.
#
# The column had never been read. It was opened because at Zora Kalanj's 1898
# baptism the godparents turned out to be the child's aunt and uncle - a kin link
# that appears nowhere else in the tree. The question was whether that is typical.
#
# It is not typical, and it is not rare either: of four consecutive children of
# one couple, two have kin as godparents and two do not, and the two alternate
# between the mother's family and the father's. So the column is worth reading
# and is NOT a reliable kinship graph. Read it for leads, never for proof.
#
# Note the officiant: Vinko Sokolic, kapelan, signs all four - and in 1900 the
# godfather is Andrij Sokolic. Parish families stand for everyone, which is
# exactly why a shared surname in this column proves nothing on its own.
#
# child_mid | child | date | godparents | relationship to the child | how known
4503765|Ana Kalanj|5 NOV 1894|Ivan i Lucija Peričić|mother's family — her mother is Marija rodj. Peričić|surname match, mother's own
4503763|Franciska Kalanj|29 JUL 1896|Andrij Zoričić i Elizabeta Zanić|no known connection|neither surname appears in this household
4503751|Zora Kalanj|4 MAR 1898|Josip i Ana Defrancesco|father's sister and her husband — the child's aunt and uncle|Ana Kalanj m. Josip de Franceschi; she is Martin's sister
4503758|Ivan Kalanj|3 JAN 1900|Andrij Sokolić i Marija Matičić|no known connection|Sokolić is also the officiating chaplain's surname
4507816|Ana Kalanj|3 JAN 1864|Josephus et Anna — surname not read|not established|Klenovica N.22; the cell is faint and has not been read at sufficient magnification
